# Scroll-Reveal & Lazy Load on Subpages

## 1. Scroll-Reveal (Primary)

Wrap each section in `AnimateOnScroll` so content reveals as the user scrolls down. Do NOT wrap the entire page in one animation — each section should animate independently when it enters the viewport.

```tsx
import { AnimateOnScroll } from "@/components/AnimateOnScroll";

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <div>
      <AnimateOnScroll variant="fade-up">
        <section>...</section>
      </AnimateOnScroll>
      <AnimateOnScroll variant="fade-up">
        <section>...</section>
      </AnimateOnScroll>
    </div>
  );
}
```

For grids/cards, use `AnimateChildren` for staggered child animation:
```tsx
<AnimateChildren className="grid ..." stagger={80}>
  {items.map((item) => <Card key={item.id} {...item} />)}
</AnimateChildren>
```

## 2. Code-Split Heavy Components

Use `next/dynamic` for large components (carousels, charts) so they load only when the page is visited:

```tsx
const HeavyComponent = dynamic(
  () => import("@/components/HeavyComponent").then((m) => ({ default: m.HeavyComponent })),
  { ssr: true, loading: () => <div className="min-h-[200px] animate-pulse rounded-xl bg-surface-alt" /> }
);
```
